course: dictionary
lesson: 10304
title: Tourist: a visitor
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a noun or an adjective, so look at how it is used. The context tells you which one it is. «Deer bow to tourists in Japan» uses tourists as a noun, the people who visit a place. Look for clues like visiting, trips and sights.
explain: A tourist is a person who travels to a place for fun, to see it and visit its sights. Here the deer bow to visitors, not to the people who live in Japan, so a tourist is a visitor. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check: «Deer bow to visitors in Japan» still makes sense.
explain: Tourist can also describe a place. A tourist town is one that many visitors come to, like a tourist attraction. Words like «tourist season» and «tourist information» follow the same pattern: they are about visitors.
fact: A tourist is a person who travels to a place for fun, to see it and visit its sights.
fact: A tourist place is one that many visitors come to, so tourist can also be an adjective: «a tourist town».
fact: Tourists often take photos, buy souvenirs and use maps and guides.
fact: Useful phrases: «tourist attraction», «tourist information» and «tourist season».
fact: Tourism brings money to towns, which is why many places want visitors.
exercise: «Rhesus macaques really live wild in China and quickly learn to grab food and phones from tourists.» Who are the tourists in this sentence? | Keepers who look after the monkeys | Monkeys that live in the trees | *People who travel to a place to see its sights | Wild boar in the parks
exercise: What does «tourist attraction» mean? | *A place that many visitors come to see | A kind of map of the mountains | A person who lives in the town | A long, quiet walk
exercise: In «a tourist town», what does tourist describe? | The person who runs the shop | *The town, because many visitors come to it | The bus that goes to the town | The sky above the town
test: «Deer bow to tourists in Japan.» What does tourist mean here? | A deer that lives in Japan | A Japanese shopkeeper | A bowing dance | *A person visiting Japan for fun, to see its sights
test: Which word means a person who travels to a place for fun? | Keeper | Macaque | *Tourist | Boar
exam: «Tourist season» most likely means what? | *A time of year when many visitors come to a place | A time of year when it snows a lot | A time of year when schools are closed | A time when the shops shut early
